# Frontend environment -- the TRINETRA dashboard lane.
#
# Copy to .env.local and edit. .env.local is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# EVERY VITE_ VARIABLE IS INLINED INTO THE PUBLIC BROWSER BUNDLE AT BUILD TIME.
# Never put a credential here. The repository is public and so is the bundle,
# and removing a value later does not remove it from a clone already made.
#
# Backend, database, ingest and model-hub keys are NOT here. They belong in the
# root .env.example, which is Mihir's per REPOSITORY 5.1. Vite reads nothing but
# VITE_ variables, so this file carries only what this app can actually use.

# ---- required (Canonical Contracts 8.1) -------------------------------------
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
VITE_WS_BASE_URL=ws://localhost:8000

# Mode: mock | api | demo
#
#   mock   MSW intercepts every request. No backend needed.
#   api    NO MSW. Every request goes to VITE_API_BASE_URL.
#   demo   MSW plus a deterministic fixture set, for rehearsals.
#
# Ships as `mock` deliberately. See the note at the bottom of this file before
# changing it -- the value the contract ships is not the value you want.
VITE_APP_MODE=mock

# ---- optional, frontend-only, NOT in contract 8.1 ---------------------------
# Both default to the first listed value. Leave them commented out unless you
# specifically need them; they exist for this lane and no other.
#
#   VITE_BASEMAP=osm|offline           osm draws tiles from the network.
#                                      offline requires public/tiles/ to be
#                                      seeded first -- procedure is in
#                                      docs/demo/RECOVERY.md. Setting this to
#                                      offline without seeding gives a blank map.
#
#   VITE_MOCK_SHAPE=canonical|hostile  hostile serves deliberately drifted
#                                      payloads -- database column names on the
#                                      wire, absent lat/lon, a camera status
#                                      outside the contract's CHECK -- to prove
#                                      the adapters absorb them. Rehearsal only;
#                                      never for a demo run.
#
# VITE_BASEMAP=osm
# VITE_MOCK_SHAPE=canonical

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE YOU CHANGE VITE_APP_MODE
#
# Contract 8.1 ships `VITE_APP_MODE=auto`. Nothing in 8.1, in 8.4, or anywhere
# else in the contract defines what `auto` resolves to. There is no rule to
# follow, so this app resolves it to `mock` and logs a warning saying so:
#
#   [trinetra] VITE_APP_MODE=auto has no defined resolution rule ...
#   [trinetra] mode=auto, mock layer ON, api base http://localhost:8000
#
# THE TRAP: copy `auto` unchanged and you are reading MOCK DATA while believing
# you are live. Every screen fills with plausible fixtures, every number looks
# reasonable, and nothing on the page indicates a problem. That failure is
# silent and it survives a demo rehearsal.
#
# This file therefore ships `mock`, which is honest about what you get. Set
# `api` when you want the dashboard talking to a real backend.
#
# Confirm which mode you actually got from the boot line in the browser console.
# It must read `mock layer OFF`, with no `[MSW] Mocking enabled` line after it,
# before you believe anything on screen came from a backend.
# See docs/demo/INTEGRATION.md for the full first-connection checklist.
#
# ALL VITE_ VARIABLES ARE INLINED AT BUILD TIME. Changing one requires another
# `npm run build` -- editing this file and restarting `npm run preview` changes
# nothing at all. Under `npm run dev` Vite restarts itself on change.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
